.Dd October 17, 2026
.Dt PATINA-BAR 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm patina-bar
.Nd the Patina desktop's bar
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl c Ar config.toml
.Nm
.Fl h | V
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the bar along the bottom (or top) of the screen.
Its buttons and icons open the launcher and the tray's menus, its tabs are
the list of open windows, and its config file holds the settings the whole
shell shares: the skin and the wallpaper.
.Pp
It holds modules on the left, in the centre and on the right:
.Bl -tag -width launcher
.It Ic launcher
The Sector F flask, which opens the launcher.
.It Ic windows
A tab per open window.
A click focuses it, a middle click closes it; the compositor's Alt+Tab
and Super+1 to 9 follow the same order.
.It Ic tray
Wi-Fi, which opens
.Xr patina-wifi 1 ;
the speaker, which opens
.Xr patina-volume 1 ;
and the battery, red at 10% or less while discharging.
.It Ic clock
The time.
.It Ic tags , layout , title , appid
dwl's status, when the bar is dwl's status command.
.El
.Pp
It's started by
.Xr patina-compositor 1 ,
and started again whenever it exits.
It runs on any compositor with wlr-layer-shell, and as dwl's status
command
.Pq Ql dwl -s patina-bar ,
reading dwl's status from its standard input.
.Pp
The menus and the launcher are opened with the bar's skin and edge in
.Ev PATINA_SKIN
and
.Ev PATINA_BAR_EDGE .
Under
.Xr patina-compositor 1
they're started by the compositor, so they're listed with their output in
Settings' Processes page; anywhere else the bar starts them itself.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl c , -config Ar file
Read
.Ar file
instead of
.Pa ~/.config/patina-bar/config.toml .
.It Fl h , -help
Print a short usage message.
.It Fl V , -version
Print the version.
.El
.Sh CONFIGURATION
.Pa ~/.config/patina-bar/config.toml ,
TOML; every key is optional.
The bar reads it again within a second of a change, and the other pieces
read it when they open.
.Xr patina-menu 1
and
.Xr patina-settings 1
write
.Ic skin
and
.Ic wallpaper ,
keeping the rest of the file.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic position
.Dq bottom
(the default) or
.Dq top .
.It Ic height
In logical pixels; 41 by default.
.It Ic skin
A Patina skin by name: a built-in, or one in
.Pa ~/.config/patina-bar/skins .
.It Ic left , center , right
The modules on each side, as lists:
.Dl left = [\(dqlauncher\(dq, \(dqwindows\(dq]
.It Ic clock
A
.Xr strftime 3
format;
.Dq %a %-d %b  %H:%M
by default.
.It Ic launcher , volume , wifi
What the flask, the speaker and the Wi-Fi icon run, through
.Xr sh 1 .
.It Ic wallpaper
An image file, drawn by
.Xr patina-wallpaper 1 ;
empty for the default.
.It Ic tags , hide_vacant_tags
A label per dwl tag, and whether to hide tags with no windows.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev PATINA_SKIN , PATINA_BAR_EDGE
Set for what the bar opens: its skin, and
.Dq top
or
.Dq bottom .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ~/.config/patina-bar/config.toml
The settings above.
.It Pa ~/.config/patina-bar/skins/
Skins of your own.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Restart the bar after installing a new one; the compositor starts it
again:
.Pp
.Dl $ pkill -x patina-bar
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr patina-compositor 1 ,
.Xr patina-volume 1 ,
.Xr patina-wallpaper 1 ,
.Xr patina-wifi 1 ,
.Xr patina-desktop 7
